<main>

<!-- ================================================================
     SECTION 1 — THE BUILD
     ================================================================ -->
<section class="sec hero" id="build">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">

    <p class="eyebrow">Case Study 02 · WordPress Flagship</p>
    <h1>SABINORA<em>Timeless elegance, engineered</em></h1>
    <p class="sub">
      A luxury label can't be judged on a marketplace listing. We built SABINORA an
      <b>editorial flagship</b> — where the art direction sets the price, the trust pages close the
      sale, and the analytics finally prove where the customers come from.
    </p>

    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip g">WordPress</span>
      <span class="chip g">WooCommerce</span>
      <span class="chip">Elementor Pro</span>
      <span class="chip">WoodMart</span>
      <span class="chip">Design System</span>
      <span class="chip">GTM + GA4 + Meta</span>
      <span class="chip">Mobile-first</span>
      <span class="chip chip-flag">Bangladesh <svg class="flag" viewBox="0 0 20 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="20" height="12" rx="1.6" fill="#006A4E"/><circle cx="8.4" cy="6" r="4.1" fill="#F42A41"/></svg></span>
    </div>
    </div><!-- /.hero-copy -->

    <div class="hero-visual">
    <!-- ---------- 3D CONCEPT #1: fanned lookbook stack ---------- -->
    <div class="stage3d" id="stage" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="glow"></div>
      <div class="stack" id="stack">
        <div class="panel p3"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="" ></div>
        <div class="panel p2"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt=""></div>
        <div class="panel base">
          <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SABINORA storefront hero — ALVARA campaign with editorial serif lockup" width="1150" height="719">
          <div class="vlabel">
            <b>ALVARA</b>
            <small>Hero campaign · 1440px capture</small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="floatwrap">
        <div class="floatcard f1"><small>Canvas token</small><b>#0B1F1C</b></div>
        <div class="floatcard f2"><small>Layout stability</small><b>CLS 0.001</b></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="stack-hint">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 9l-3 3 3 3M9 5l3-3 3 3M15 19l-3 3-3-3M19 9l3 3-3 3"/></svg>
    </p>
    </div><!-- /.hero-visual -->
    </div><!-- /.hero-grid -->

    <div class="stats" role="list">
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="5" role="listitem">5</b><span>Collections</span></div>
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>#0B1F1C</b><span>Signature canvas</span></div>
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="7">7</b><span>Trust pages</span></div>
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="3">3</b><span>Tracking stacks</span></div>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- design system ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:54px">
      <span class="kicker">The design system</span>
      <h2>One canvas colour, held with discipline</h2>
      <p class="lede">The entire brand sits on a single deep emerald — <b>#0B1F1C</b> — used more than
        500 times across the homepage. Everything else is a deliberate exception: cream for readability,
        gold for value, blush for warmth. That restraint is what reads as "expensive".</p>
    </div>

    <div class="palette" aria-label="SABINORA design tokens">
      <div class="sw s1"><b>Canvas</b><small>#0B1F1C · 549 uses</small></div>
      <div class="sw s2"><b>Canvas deep</b><small>#153532</small></div>
      <div class="sw s3"><b>Cream type</b><small>#F3EFE7</small></div>
      <div class="sw s4"><b>Gold accent</b><small>#C8A96B</small></div>
      <div class="sw s5"><b>Jade mid</b><small>#3E8C7A</small></div>
      <div class="sw s6"><b>Blush</b><small>#E7C3CE</small></div>
      <div class="sw wide">
        <span style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:14px">Playfair Display as the primary face</span>
        <small style="color:var(--ink-3)">Serif-first typography is the whole brand voice</small>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- what shipped ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:54px">
      <span class="kicker">What shipped</span>
      <h2>A storefront that behaves like a <em>lookbook</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">Capsule drops, not a warehouse. Four products on the homepage, five collections,
        one campaign film — and the layout never once looks empty.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g3">
      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M3 15l5-5 4 4 3-3 6 6"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Art direction</span>
        <h4>Full-bleed editorial heroes</h4>
        <p>Each slide is a campaign frame with a serif product lockup — <b>ALVARA</b>, <b>ELORIA</b> — and a
          poetic product line. The same art direction survives intact on a 390px phone.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="18" rx="1.5"/><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="18" rx="1.5"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Navigation</span>
        <h4>Masked collection tiles</h4>
        <p>Five collections — Embroidered Treasures, The Silk Narrative, The Couture Pret, The Debut Drop,
          The Cotton Collective — as image-masked cards with live product counts and hover reveals.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M10 9l5 3-5 3z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Campaign</span>
        <h4>Lightbox campaign film</h4>
        <p>"SOVEREIGN SILK — Volume I — Introducing SERAPHINE" plays in a lightbox over a poster image,
          so the launch video never costs the page a single embed on load.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M4 4h16v12H7l-3 3z"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 12h5"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Capture</span>
        <h4>Newsletter with consent copy</h4>
        <p>An inline capture block with its own privacy-policy line — the list is the only marketing asset
          a fashion brand truly owns, so it gets a designed, permanent slot.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 2l8 4v6c0 5-3.4 8.6-8 10-4.6-1.4-8-5-8-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Trust</span>
        <h4>Seven policy pages, zero guesswork</h4>
        <p>Shipping &amp; Payment, Return/Exchange/Refund, Terms, Privacy, FAQ, Careers and a dedicated
          <b>Complaint Center</b>. For BD online fashion, published policy <em>is</em> the conversion asset.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M3 20V10M9 20V4M15 20v-7M21 20V7"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Measurement</span>
        <h4>GTM + GA4 + Meta pixel</h4>
        <p>Google Tag Manager <code>GTM-KQNSMT8X</code> feeding GA4 <code>G-678R6GH8FL</code>, with
          PixelYourSite handling the Meta pixel. Ad spend can now be judged, not guessed.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- evidence ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:56px">
      <span class="kicker">Evidence · live captures</span>
      <h2>Straight from production</h2>
      <p class="lede">Captured at 1440px desktop and 390px mobile on the live site. Tap any plate to enlarge.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <figure class="plate rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Top Visited Categories — five collections as masked image cards with product counts">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SABINORA collection tiles with masked imagery" loading="lazy" width="1100" height="280">
        <figcaption><em>Home</em> Masked collection tiles · 5 collections</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="plate rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Sovereign Silk, Volume I — the SERAPHINE campaign film delivered as a lightbox over a poster image">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SABINORA Sovereign Silk campaign film block" loading="lazy" width="900" height="507">
        <figcaption><em>Campaign</em> Lightbox film · no embed cost on load</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="plate plate-device rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Mobile 390px — full-bleed editorial hero preserved, 4-tab sticky bottom navigation">
        <div class="device-stage">
          <div class="phone">
            <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SABINORA mobile storefront with sticky bottom navigation" loading="lazy" width="560" height="1150">
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><em>Mobile</em> Art direction intact · 4-tab tab bar</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="plate rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Desktop 1440px — the ALVARA hero: campaign photography, serif lockup, poetic product line">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SABINORA ALVARA hero section on desktop" loading="lazy" width="1150" height="719">
        <figcaption><em>Hero</em> ALVARA lockup · full-bleed campaign</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- architecture ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:56px">
      <span class="kicker">Build architecture</span>
      <h2>Five layers, each with one job</h2>
      <p class="lede">Built on Elementor Pro so the client team can edit campaigns without a developer —
        but every layer below was configured deliberately rather than left to plugin defaults.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3D CONCEPT #2: layered system stack -->
    <div class="layers3d" id="layers" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="layers">
        <div class="layer"><span class="n">L1</span><h4>Presentation</h4><p>Elementor Pro widget kit — masked category loop, product rails, toggle accordions, slides, lightbox video</p></div>
        <div class="layer"><span class="n">L2</span><h4>Design system</h4><p>#0B1F1C canvas, cream type scale, Playfair Display primary face, gold accent token, full-bleed <code>wrapper-custom</code> grid</p></div>
        <div class="layer"><span class="n">L3</span><h4>Commerce</h4><p>WooCommerce 8.4.1 — AJAX filter drawer, price ranges (৳990–1,499), variation swatches, wishlist, COD checkout</p></div>
        <div class="layer"><span class="n">L4</span><h4>Trust</h4><p>Seven policy pages, Complaint Center, WhatsApp line, FB/IG/YouTube-Shorts presence, newsletter consent copy</p></div>
        <div class="layer"><span class="n">L5</span><h4>Measurement</h4><p>GTM container → GA4 property + Meta pixel via PixelYourSite, with consent-friendly markup baked in</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:22px">
      <div class="code rv">
        <div class="h"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>tracking · verified in page source</span></div>
<pre><span class="c">// Google Tag Manager container (head + body)</span>
gtm_id: <span class="s">"GTM-KQNSMT8X"</span>

<span class="c">// GA4 property wired through the container</span>
measurement_id: <span class="s">"G-678R6GH8FL"</span>

<span class="c">// Meta pixel served by PixelYourSite</span>
facebook_sdk: { lang: <span class="s">"en_US"</span>, app_id: <span class="s">""</span> }

<span class="c">// WooCommerce endpoints exposed to the tag layer</span>
cart_page_url:     <span class="t">/cart/</span>
checkout_page_url: <span class="t">/checkout/</span></pre>
        <div class="code-cap"><b>Three stacks, one funnel.</b> The container means new campaigns can be added
          without touching theme code — and every Add-to-Cart event lands in one place.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card rv" style="padding:22px">
        <h4 style="font-size:15px;font-family:var(--sans)">Design decisions that did the selling</h4>
        <ul class="ulist">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Dark canvas, bright product.</b> Photography reads brighter and more premium against
            #0B1F1C than against white — the same trick a gallery uses with dark walls.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Serif as the brand voice.</b> Playfair Display carries every headline, so a ৳999 piece and
            a ৳1,499 piece sit in the same considered world.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Video behind a poster.</b> The launch film loads as an image until clicked — the page
            keeps its speed and the film keeps its impact.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Mobile art direction, not mobile fallback.</b> The hero is re-composed for 390px rather
            than cropped down, and the four-tab bottom bar keeps Shop and Wishlist one thumb away.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================================================================
     SECTION 2 — THE IMPACT
     ================================================================ -->
<section class="sec impact" id="impact">
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="kicker">Section 02 · Why this site · Why it matters</span>
      <h2>Luxury isn't a price. It's <em>certainty</em>.</h2>
      <p class="lede">When a shopper can't touch the fabric, every other signal has to carry the promise:
        the typography, the photography, the return policy, the phone number, the loading speed.
        SABINORA's job was to make a first-time visitor <b>believe</b> before she believes the price tag.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ps">
      <article class="psrow rv">
        <div class="p">
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Problem</span>
          <h4>Marketplace shelves flatten premium brands</h4>
          <p>On a shared listings page, a hand-finished piece looks exactly like a mass-market one — so it
            gets compared on price alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s">
          <div class="arw"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12l7 7 7-7"/></svg></div>
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Solution</span>
          <h4>An owned editorial flagship</h4>
          <p>Full-bleed campaign heroes, named collections and a serif voice that frames the brand before
            the price is ever shown.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="psrow rv">
        <div class="p">
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Problem</span>
          <h4>Nobody trusts an online store with no paperwork</h4>
          <p>In BD fashion, the fear isn't the price — it's "will it arrive, will it fit, can I return it,
            who do I shout at if it doesn't?"</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s">
          <div class="arw"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12l7 7 7-7"/></svg></div>
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Solution</span>
          <h4>Trust architecture, published</h4>
          <p>Seven policy pages including a dedicated Complaint Center, a WhatsApp line, live social
            channels and COD checkout — doubt answered before it's formed.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="psrow rv">
        <div class="p">
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Problem</span>
          <h4>Ad spend with no way to judge it</h4>
          <p>Traffic arrived from Facebook and search, and nobody could say which post or which collection
            actually produced an order.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s">
          <div class="arw"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12l7 7 7-7"/></svg></div>
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Solution</span>
          <h4>A full measurement funnel</h4>
          <p>GTM container feeding GA4 and the Meta pixel, with WooCommerce cart and checkout endpoints
            exposed to the tag layer — every campaign is now accountable.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- 3D CONCEPT #3: vitals -->
    <div class="chartwrap" id="chart">
      <div class="chart-title">
        <h4>Measured on the live site</h4>
        <span>cold cache · headless Chromium · 2026-10-02</span>
      </div>
      <p class="chart-note">Two numbers matter most in a luxury build: the layout must never flinch while
        it loads, and the first campaign frame must arrive fast enough to hold attention.</p>
      <div class="bars3d" id="bars">
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:12%"><span class="val">0.001</span><div class="fill jade"></div></div><span class="lbl">CLS</span></div>
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:56%"><span class="val">1,010</span><div class="fill"></div></div><span class="lbl">DOM nodes</span></div>
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:42%"><span class="val">2.1 s</span><div class="fill blush"></div></div><span class="lbl">FCP desk</span></div>
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:82%"><span class="val">6.0 s</span><div class="fill"></div></div><span class="lbl">LCP desk</span></div>
      </div>
      <div style="height:30px"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:16px">
      <div class="card rv">
        <h4 style="font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600">Layout stability of 0.001</h4>
        <p>Effectively zero movement. Measurement IDs, campaign imagery and third-party tags all load
          without nudging the layout — visitors never lose their place mid-scroll, on either device.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card rv">
        <h4 style="font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600">1,010 DOM nodes — 48% leaner</h4>
        <p>Half the markup of its sibling build for the same visual richness. Fewer nodes means faster
          rendering on the mid-range Android phones most BD traffic arrives on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card rv">
        <h4 style="font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600">Capsule economy, zero empty shelves</h4>
        <p>Four hero products, five collections and one campaign film are composed to fill the page
          completely — a new label looks established from day one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- roadmap -->
    <div class="road">
      <div class="roadcol now rv">
        <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Shipped &amp; verified</h4>
        <ul class="rlist">
          <li><b>Editorial design system</b> — #0B1F1C canvas, cream scale, Playfair Display voice, gold accent token.</li>
          <li><b>Campaign-led homepage</b> — full-bleed heroes with serif product lockups, preserved on mobile.</li>
          <li><b>Masked collection navigation</b> — five collections with live counts and hover reveals.</li>
          <li><b>Lightbox campaign film</b> — Sovereign Silk / SERAPHINE with a poster-first load.</li>
          <li><b>Trust architecture</b> — seven policy pages, Complaint Center, WhatsApp, COD, live socials.</li>
          <li><b>Full measurement stack</b> — GTM-KQNSMT8X → GA4 G-678R6GH8FL + Meta pixel via PixelYourSite.</li>
          <li><b>Layout stability at 0.001 CLS</b> on both desktop and mobile — measured, not assumed.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="roadcol next rv">
        <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Next sprint (our own audit)</h4>
        <ul class="rlist">
          <li><b>Fix the LCP.</b> 6.0s desktop / 4.6s mobile is the top priority — convert the heavy PNGs to WebP/AVIF and preload the first campaign frame.</li>
          <li><b>Defer third-party scripts.</b> googletagmanager (927 KB) and connect.facebook.net (797 KB) currently load eagerly; both can be delayed until first interaction.</li>
          <li><b>Fill the "Reels" section.</b> The heading ships next to an empty container — either populate it from the YouTube Shorts channel or remove the section.</li>
          <li><b>Add an H1 and meta descriptions.</b> Home and Shop ship no H1; no page has a meta description.</li>
          <li><b>Set a social share image.</b> No og:image means Facebook shares — the main discovery channel for BD fashion — render as a bare link.</li>
          <li><b>Alt text to 100%</b> — currently 90% of homepage images are unnamed.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- outcome -->
    <div class="outcome rv">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px">The outcome</p>
          <h3>A label with a flagship — and the numbers to grow it.</h3>
          <p>SABINORA now presents its collections the way a fashion house should: campaign imagery, a
            consistent editorial voice, collections with names instead of SKUs, and published answers to
            every question a first-time BD buyer asks. Behind it, a measurement funnel turns ad spend into
            something you can actually judge. And because the layout is rock-solid at 0.001 CLS and the
            markup is 48% leaner than a comparable build, it stays fast while the catalogue grows.</p>
          <div class="btnrow">
            <a class="btn btn-p" href="https://sabinorabd.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/><path d="M15 3h6v6M10 14 21 3"/></svg>
              View live site
            </a>
            <a class="btn btn-g" href="#build">Back to top</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stats" style="margin:0;border-color:var(--line);background:rgba(200,169,107,.10)">
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b>5</b><span>Collections</span></div>
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b>7</b><span>Trust pages</span></div>
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b>0.001</b><span>CLS</span></div>
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b>3</b><span>Tracking stacks</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

</main>

